Wan2.2
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything under `wan/` is derived from Alibaba's Wan2.2 and remains under the Apache
License 2.0. The original copyright headers are retained in place. Files carrying

    Copyright 2024-2025 The Alibaba Wan Team Authors. All rights reserved.

are either unmodified copies or modified versions of upstream Wan2.2 sources.

Modifications made by this project, relative to upstream Wan2.2:

* `wan/modules/causal_model.py` — added block-causal attention with a KV cache, the
  rolling-forcing attention path (sliding window + attention sink), and a ControlNet
  side branch (`CausalControlNet`, `CausalControlledWanModel`).
* `wan/modules/model.py` — added the bidirectional ControlNet side branch (`ControlNet`,
  `ControlledWanModel`) used by the teacher.
* `wan/modules/attention.py` — FlashAttention-3 support alongside FA2, including
  handling both the tuple and bare-tensor return shapes of
  `flash_attn_interface.flash_attn_varlen_func`.
* `wan/utils/utils.py` — reduced to `masks_like`, the only helper this project calls.
* `wan/__init__.py`, `wan/modules/__init__.py`, `wan/utils/__init__.py` — reduced to
  the subset this project imports; the upstream barrels eagerly imported model
  variants that are not part of this release.
* Removed from this distribution: the animate, speech-to-video, image-to-video,
  text-to-video and text+image-to-video pipelines, the distributed (FSDP / Ulysses /
  sequence-parallel) helpers, the Wan2.1 VAE, the prompt-extension utilities, and the
  video/image saving and CosyVoice download helpers from `wan/utils/utils.py`.
  None of them are reachable from this project's entry points. They remain available
  upstream.

